## Criteria the build must meet (from the issue, word for word)
1. packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js <file> prints <file>:<line>: <error> for every row that is not valid JSON (1-based lines, blank lines skipped, an unterminated last line checked) and exits 1 if any, 0 if none
2. A missing file or no argument prints to stderr and exits 2
3. packages/jsonl-lint/src/index.js exports lint(text) returning [{ line, error }]
4. The workspace has its own package.json (jsonl-lint, type module, test script node --test), no runtime dependencies, and node:test tests for a clean file, a bad middle row, a torn last row, blank lines and the exit codes
5. packages/jsonl-lint/README.md exists and the root README lists the tool
6. The change is one PR on suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test whose body says Closes https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102, and npm test and the test workflow are green at its head

## Steps
1. Read CLAUDE.md, README.md, package.json and .github/workflows/test.yml at the repository root. `packages/` does not exist yet; the root `npm test` runs `npm test --workspaces --if-present` over `packages/*`, and CI runs `npm ci` then `npm test` on Node 22.
2. Create packages/jsonl-lint/package.json: `"name": "jsonl-lint"`, `"type": "module"`, `"scripts": { "test": "node --test" }`, a `bin` entry `{ "jsonl-lint": "bin/jsonl-lint.js" }`, `engines.node >=22`, and no `dependencies` field (no devDependencies either; only Node built-ins).
3. Create packages/jsonl-lint/src/index.js, a plain ES module that exports `lint(text)`:
   - Split on `\n` (strip a trailing `\r` per row so CRLF files work). Line numbers are 1-based and count every physical line, blank ones included.
   - Skip lines that are empty or whitespace only.
   - `JSON.parse` every other line, including a last line with no trailing newline (a torn/unterminated last row must be reported if it is not valid JSON). A trailing newline at end of file must not produce an extra error.
   - Return an array of `{ line, error }` (error = the parse error message string), in line order; `[]` when all rows are valid.
4. Create packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js with a `#!/usr/bin/env node` shebang (and mark it executable, `chmod +x`, committed with mode 100755):
   - No argument: print a usage message to stderr, exit 2.
   - File cannot be read (missing, etc.): print an error to stderr, exit 2.
   - Otherwise read the file as UTF-8, call `lint`, and print one line per error to stdout exactly in the form `<file>:<line>: <error>`, where `<file>` is the path argument as given. Exit 1 if there were any errors, 0 if none (print nothing on success to stdout).
   - Set `process.exitCode` rather than calling `process.exit()` right after writing, so output is not truncated.
5. Write node:test tests under packages/jsonl-lint/test/ (e.g. `test/lint.test.js`, `test/cli.test.js`; `node --test` run from packages/jsonl-lint must discover them). Cover at least: a clean file (no errors, CLI exit 0, empty stdout); a bad middle row (reported with the right 1-based line, CLI exit 1, stdout line `<file>:<line>: ...`); a torn last row with no trailing newline (reported); blank lines (skipped and not reported, while line numbers after them stay correct); and the exit codes 0, 1, 2 (2 for no argument and for a missing file, with a message on stderr). Drive the CLI with `child_process.spawnSync(process.execPath, [binPath, ...])` and temp files from `fs.mkdtempSync(os.tmpdir())`; resolve paths from `import.meta.url` so tests work from any cwd.
6. Write packages/jsonl-lint/README.md: what it does, usage (`node packages/jsonl-lint/bin/jsonl-lint.js <file>`), output format, exit codes 0/1/2, the `lint(text)` API, and how to run tests.
7. Update the root README.md: replace the "No tools yet" bullet under "What is here" with an entry listing `packages/jsonl-lint` and a one-line description linking to its README.
8. From the repository root run `npm install` so package-lock.json picks up the new workspace (CI uses `npm ci`, which fails if the lock file is out of sync), then run `npm ci` and `npm test` and make sure both succeed. Commit package-lock.json with the change.
9. Open exactly one pull request on suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test with all of the above. The PR body must contain the line `Closes https://github.com/suredesigntshirts/ccp_machine_test/issues/102`. Wait for the `test` workflow to finish on the PR head commit and confirm it is green; if it fails, fix it on the same branch and push until it is green.